{
  "summary": "Adds two USDT tracepoints to P2P processing: `net:block_header`, which triggers when a new valid header arrives via a `headers` or `cmpctblock` message, and `net:compact_block_reconstructed`, which fires when a compact block is successfully reconstructed before validation. It encapsulates compact block reconstruction statistics into a helper struct on `PartiallyDownloadedBlock` and adds functional BPF test coverage.",
  "problem": "Compact block relay performance and diagnostics rely on string-based debug logs (`BCLog::CMPCTBLOCK`), which are awkward to parse reliably in external tooling, cannot easily be monitored continuously in production without log parsing overhead, and make attributing relay efficiency to specific peers difficult.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes that whether a node reconstructs a block without round trips depends on mempool overlap, extra transaction pool usefulness, and peer behavior, but today 'this information is mostly available only through debug logs, which are string-based, less precise for tooling, and not ideal for continuous measurement.'"
  ],
